/// Behavioral API documentation for the CEFR Master backend.
/// Static Markdown authored from the current backend source.
mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# CEFR Master Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister stores and serves the CEFR Master English-course platform: mock tests, reading passages, listening items, speaking cards, writing prompts, external links and announcements, plus each signed-in student's saved dictionary words and writing drafts.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- Content reads (`listTests`, `getTest`, `listPassages`, `getPassage`, `listListening`, `getListening`, `listSpeakingCards`, `getSpeakingCard`, `listWritingPrompts`, `getWritingPrompt`, `listLinks`, `getLink`, `listAnnouncements`, `getAnnouncement`, `exportContent`) are public queries and need no sign-in.\n- Content writes (`upsert*`, `delete*`, `importContent`) require the caller to hold the `admin` role. A non-admin caller traps with `Unauthorized: admin role required`.\n- `checkAdminPasscode(passcode)` is a public query that returns `true` when the passcode matches the stored hash. It does not itself grant the admin role; the frontend uses it to unlock the admin dashboard, and the canister separately enforces the admin role on writes.\n- Student endpoints (`listSavedWords`, `saveWord`, `removeSavedWord`, `listDrafts`, `getDraft`, `saveDraft`, `deleteDraft`) are keyed to the caller principal. They are callable by any caller, including anonymous ones, but each principal sees only its own data.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration: the first caller to invoke `_initialize_access_control` becomes the admin; subsequent callers receive the `user` role. A caller that never signed in through the app's own frontend is unregistered even if it belongs to the app's owner, and a principal derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. An unregistered caller receives `Unauthorized: admin role required` on every content write.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `Timestamp` is a signed nanosecond value (`Time.now()`).\n- `Id` is a `Nat`. Passing `id = 0` to any `upsert*` allocates a new id; passing an existing id replaces that record.\n- `CefrLevel` is the variant `#b1 | #b2 | #c1`; `Skill` is `#reading | #listening | #speaking | #writing | #grammar | #vocabulary`.\n- `exportContent` returns the whole content set as a JSON text document; `importContent` accepts the same shape.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- All reads are `query` calls and return immediately.\n- Writes are update calls; the frontend should refetch the affected list after a successful write rather than poll.\n- `importContent` replaces the entire content set atomically in one message.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `upsert*` is idempotent for a given id: repeating the same call leaves the same record.\n- `delete*` returns `false` when the id does not exist and `true` when it was removed; repeating a delete is safe.\n- `saveWord` and `saveDraft` are idempotent upserts keyed by word text and prompt id respectively.\n- `importContent` is destructive: it clears the existing content before loading the bundle. Retrying it with the same JSON is safe; retrying with a different bundle replaces the content again.\n\n## Errors and gotchas\n\n- Content writes from a non-admin caller trap; the frontend must surface this as an authorization failure, not a validation error.\n- `importContent` traps on malformed JSON.\n- Student data is isolated per principal; an anonymous caller has its own empty namespace and cannot read another principal's words or drafts.\n";
  };
};
